  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MAINTAINING BLACK RHINO SECURITY AND MONITORING IN THE CHYULU HILLS, KENYA - 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO SUPPORT A CONSERVATION EFFORT IN THE NATIONAL PARK AND COMMUNITY LAND OF CHYULU HILLS, KENYABY CONTINUING TO IMPROVE RHINOCEROS MONITORINGAND SECURITY FOR FUTURE EFFORTS TO EXPAND THE POPULATION AS RECOMMENDED IN KENYA SBLACK RHINOCEROS ACTION PLAN. THIS PROJECT IS INTENDED TO CONSERVE THE EASTERN BLACK RHINOCEROS AND THEIR HABITAT BY ADDRESSING THE IMPACTS OFPOACHING, HUMAN ENCROACHMENT,AND INADEQUATE SECURE HABITAT. SPECIFIC ACTIVITIES INCLUDE (1) INCREASING RHINOCEROS MONITORING AND (2) IMPROVING SECURITY.</narrative>
  </description>
